WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.020
It was only a matter of time before Chris
Pratt became an A-list movie star.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.480
He's now at the center of multiple franchises
— he's Star-Lord in Guardians of the Galaxy,

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.599
Owen in Jurassic World, and Emmett in The
Lego Movie.

00:00:11.599 --> 00:00:15.950
But Pratt slowly built up his career with
regular roles on TV and supporting roles in

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:18.760
big-screen productions before earning his
spot on the top.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:22.780
Throughout it all, Pratt has proven to be
a charming, entertaining, and most of all,

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:23.600
hilarious guy.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.120
Here are some times that the camera captured
him on movie and TV sets goofing off, screwing

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.120
up, and ad-libbing.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:30.800
The O.C.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.560
One of Pratt's earliest roles was playing
Ché on Fox's teen soap The O.C..

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.580
And while the part mostly required him to
act like a burnout, he did seem to have a

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.700
lot of fun with it … until he had to eat
on-camera, that is.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:46.940
In one scene, he was supposed to be giving
sage advice to Seth Cohen while eating a bowl

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:47.600
of figs.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.160
And it probably would've gone off without
a hitch if Pratt hadn't grabbed a spoiled

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:51.760
piece of fruit.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:56.080
"I'm sorry.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.700
This one's a bad one."

00:00:58.940 --> 00:00:59.740
What's Your Number?

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.140
Wearing a fat suit might hinder some actors'
ability to bust a move, but that wasn't the

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:05.180
case for Chris Pratt.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.600
In What's Your Number?, Pratt had to bulk
up a bit, but he still managed to bust out

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:12.470
some impressively accurate Michael Jackson
dance moves that were totally uninhibited

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:13.740
by the extra poundage.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.760
He should put that on his resume.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.560
Parks and Recreation

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.740
Pratt didn't come out of nowhere to become
the biggest action hero working today.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:25.270
Before he started saving the world, he was
best known for his supporting role in NBC

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:26.900
comedy Parks and Recreation.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:31.080
But the inklings of a hero were still present
in his role as the dumb but eager man-child

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:31.820
Andy Dwyer.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:35.920
In this outtake, Pratt rapidly hurdled over
a counter and then ditched a briefcase his

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.620
character didn't need to steal by throwing
it back from where he got it.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:42.120
Amazingly, the case nailed a light switch
— and left the actors in the dark.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.700
"F------ hilarious."

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.500
"That's not something that props can fix.

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:47.460
Sorry.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:48.160
I'm out."

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:52.480
Delivery Man

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:57.420
Even though Chris Pratt was on the cusp of
mega success when he starred in this 2013

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.060
comedy, he was still pretty hungry.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.420
At least, that's all we can assume from watching
this outtake of him chasing a wad of cash

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.770
from blowing away in the wind.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.220
"Why not is that too real?

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:08.360
Is that too real?"

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.380
Jurassic World

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.140
Pratt's character, Owen, can do a lot of things.

00:02:13.349 --> 00:02:18.099
He can ride a motorcycle, he can tame velociraptors,
and he can even make the T-Rex look like a

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:18.720
good guy.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:23.080
But acting out one of Owen's talents in particular
gave Chris Pratt some trouble on the set.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:27.680
While his character was capable of doing crazy
things, Pratt had a lot of trouble whistling

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:31.439
— and the behind-the-scenes footage of his
repeated failed efforts made for some great

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:31.940
B-roll.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.440
"I'll get it."

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:37.700
Guardians of the Galaxy

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.379
Flying a spaceship is fun, and it would seem
that even pretending to fly a spaceship is

00:02:42.379 --> 00:02:46.260
also a thrill, because on the set of Guardians
of the Galaxy, Pratt got a little carried

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.380
away behind the controls of the mighty Milano.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:52.860
The filmmakers probably only really needed
a second or two of Star-Lord looking excited,

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:56.280
but Pratt got downright maniacal with his
unbridled glee.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.000
"Hahaha!"

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.340
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:10.540
The Guardians returned for some more outer
space adventures in Guardians of the Galaxy

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.340
Vol. 2, but they weren't alone.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:17.300
A few new characters came along, including
an ageless Celestial named Ego, who was also

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.080
Star-Lord's father, played by Kurt Russell.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.580
Because the movie was set on several distant
planets, gravity wasn't always a given.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:26.440
So to replicate that, the actors had to endure
a lot of "wire work."

00:03:26.629 --> 00:03:31.120
And in this outtake from the movie, Pratt
and Russell had a hard time getting the "hang"

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:31.780
of things.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:35.640
"I think we got it."

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:39.920
The film also presented another all-star blooper
when we were introduced to the High Priestess

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:40.860
of the Sovereigns.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.519
She tried to chat up the Star-Lord about breeding
techniques, and she got this as an explanation

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:46.700
of how earthlings do it:

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:52.460
"I personally control half the DNA by doing
something I call doinking."

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:54.720
Passengers

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:59.439
For a large portion his other space movie
Passengers, Chris Pratt wandered around a

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.980
gigantic ship almost entirely by himself.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:06.840
His only "human" interaction was with an android
bartender named Arthur, played by Michael

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:07.340
Sheen.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:11.200
Arthur provided drinks and a little bit of
companionship…and since there wasn't much

00:04:11.219 --> 00:04:14.739
else to do, Pratt's character was a patron
of the pub quite often.

00:04:14.739 --> 00:04:19.220
In this outtake, Pratt got a chance to do
some "drunk acting," and he comically over-reacted

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.079
to Arthur's boozy blue concoction...

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.480
"There's coconut in it?"

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.330
It's amazing none of these moments made into
the movies, really.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:31.360
Thanks for watching!

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:34.009
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:34.009 --> 00:04:36.430
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

